No stack was specified, so I'll assume a **Node/TypeScript service with Redis**. The pattern is **cache-aside**:

- **Reads** check Redis first, fall back to the DB on a miss, then populate the cache.
- **Writes** update the DB, then invalidate the cache entry.
- **TTL with jitter** so entries don't all expire at the same moment.
- **Negative caching** so repeated lookups for missing users don't hit the DB.
- **In-process request coalescing** so a burst of misses for one user triggers only one DB query.
- **Fail-open**: if Redis is down, the API still serves from the DB.

## `profileCache.ts`

```ts
import Redis from "ioredis";

export interface UserProfile {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  avatarUrl?: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}

export interface ProfileRepository {
  findById(id: string): Promise<UserProfile | null>;
  update(id: string, patch: Partial<UserProfile>): Promise<UserProfile>;
}

interface CacheOptions {
  ttlSeconds?: number;         // base TTL for found profiles
  negativeTtlSeconds?: number; // TTL for "user not found"
  jitterRatio?: number;        // e.g. 0.1 = ±10% TTL jitter
  keyPrefix?: string;
  schemaVersion?: number;      // bump to invalidate everything after a shape change
}

const NOT_FOUND = "__NOT_FOUND__";

export class CachedProfileService {
  private inflight = new Map<string, Promise<UserProfile | null>>();
  private opts: Required<CacheOptions>;

  constructor(
    private redis: Redis,
    private repo: ProfileRepository,
    opts: CacheOptions = {}
  ) {
    this.opts = {
      ttlSeconds: 300,
      negativeTtlSeconds: 30,
      jitterRatio: 0.1,
      keyPrefix: "user:profile",
      schemaVersion: 1,
      ...opts,
    };
  }

  private key(id: string) {
    return `${this.opts.keyPrefix}:v${this.opts.schemaVersion}:${id}`;
  }

  private ttl(base: number) {
    const j = base * this.opts.jitterRatio;
    return Math.max(1, Math.round(base + (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * j));
  }

  async getProfile(id: string): Promise<UserProfile | null> {
    const key = this.key(id);

    // 1. Try cache (fail open on Redis errors)
    try {
      const cached = await this.redis.get(key);
      if (cached === NOT_FOUND) return null;
      if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached) as UserProfile;
    } catch (err) {
      console.warn("profile cache read failed", { id, err });
    }

    // 2. Coalesce concurrent misses for the same id
    const existing = this.inflight.get(id);
    if (existing) return existing;

    const load = this.loadAndPopulate(id, key).finally(() =>
      this.inflight.delete(id)
    );
    this.inflight.set(id, load);
    return load;
  }

  private async loadAndPopulate(id: string, key: string) {
    const profile = await this.repo.findById(id);
    try {
      if (profile) {
        await this.redis.set(key, JSON.stringify(profile), "EX", this.ttl(this.opts.ttlSeconds));
      } else {
        await this.redis.set(key, NOT_FOUND, "EX", this.opts.negativeTtlSeconds);
      }
    } catch (err) {
      console.warn("profile cache write failed", { id, err });
    }
    return profile;
  }

  async updateProfile(id: string, patch: Partial<UserProfile>): Promise<UserProfile> {
    const updated = await this.repo.update(id, patch);
    await this.invalidate(id);
    return updated;
  }

  async invalidate(id: string): Promise<void> {
    try {
      await this.redis.del(this.key(id));
    } catch (err) {
      // If this fails, the stale entry lives at most one TTL.
      console.error("profile cache invalidation failed", { id, err });
    }
  }
}
```

## Wiring it into an Express route

```ts
import express from "express";
import Redis from "ioredis";
import { CachedProfileService } from "./profileCache";
import { pgProfileRepository } from "./db"; // your existing data access layer

const redis = new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL!, {
  maxRetriesPerRequest: 1,  // don't let a slow Redis stall requests
  enableOfflineQueue: false,
});

const profiles = new CachedProfileService(redis, pgProfileRepository, {
  ttlSeconds: 300,
});

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

app.get("/users/:id/profile", async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const profile = await profiles.getProfile(req.params.id);
    if (!profile) return res.status(404).json({ error: "Not found" });
    res.set("Cache-Control", "private, max-age=60");
    res.json(profile);
  } catch (e) { next(e); }
});

app.patch("/users/:id/profile", async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    // authz check goes here
    const updated = await profiles.updateProfile(req.params.id, req.body);
    res.json(updated);
  } catch (e) { next(e); }
});
```

## Test sketch (Vitest + ioredis-mock)

```ts
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from "vitest";
import RedisMock from "ioredis-mock";
import { CachedProfileService } from "./profileCache";

const profile = { id: "u1", name: "A", email: "a@x.io", updatedAt: "2026-01-01" };

describe("CachedProfileService", () => {
  it("hits the DB once, then serves from cache", async () => {
    const repo = { findById: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(profile), update: vi.fn() };
    const svc = new CachedProfileService(new RedisMock() as any, repo);
    await svc.getProfile("u1");
    await svc.getProfile("u1");
    expect(repo.findById).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });

  it("coalesces concurrent misses", async () => {
    const repo = { findById: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(profile), update: vi.fn() };
    const svc = new CachedProfileService(new RedisMock() as any, repo);
    await Promise.all([svc.getProfile("u1"), svc.getProfile("u1"), svc.getProfile("u1")]);
    expect(repo.findById).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });

  it("invalidates on update", async () => {
    const repo = {
      findById: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(profile),
      update: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ ...profile, name: "B" }),
    };
    const svc = new CachedProfileService(new RedisMock() as any, repo);
    await svc.getProfile("u1");
    await svc.updateProfile("u1", { name: "B" });
    await svc.getProfile("u1");
    expect(repo.findById).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);
  });
});
```

## Things to decide for your setup

- **Invalidate on every write path.** Any code that changes profiles outside `updateProfile` (admin tools, batch jobs, other services) must call `invalidate()` or publish an event that does. Otherwise you get up to one TTL of stale data.
- **Delete-after-write race.** A reader can load the old row just before the write commits and cache it after the delete runs. The TTL bounds this. If you need tighter guarantees, do a second delete a second or two later, or invalidate from a CDC/outbox event.
- **PII.** Profiles often contain email and similar fields. Use a Redis instance with auth and TLS, and consider caching only the fields the endpoint returns.
- **Multi-instance coalescing.** The `inflight` map only dedupes misses within one process. That's usually enough. For very hot keys across many pods, add a short Redis lock (`SET key NX PX 5000`) around the DB load.

